   "text": "I read the molecule as a linear acyl-peptide tail attached to a thioether-bridged macrocyclic peptide. I could not confirm the stereochemistry from the drawing alone, so I assigned L-configuration to every \u03b1-carbon, including the Cys. I did not check each wedge and hash against that assumption.\n\n**Tail (top left):**\n- A 4-iodophenyl-butanoyl group is acylated onto the \u03b1-amine of Glu1.\n- Glu1's side-chain carboxyl forms an amide with the \u03b1-amine of Glu2.\n- Glu2's side-chain carboxyl forms an amide with the \u03b1-amine of a Lys that has a C-terminal primary amide.\n- That Lys's \u03b5-amine is acylated by the Cys carbonyl, which leads into the macrocycle.\n\n**Macrocycle sequence**, starting from Cys and following the backbone:\n1. Cys, whose sulfur is joined through CH2C(=O) to the amine of Phe(4-COOH). This is the thioether bridge.\n2. Phe(4-COOH).\n3. N-methyl-Lys.\n4. Val.\n5. Val.\n6. Ser.\n7. Asn.\n8. Trp, alkylated on its indole nitrogen.\n9. Phe(4-COOH).\n10. Lys, with a free \u03b5-amine.\n11. 5-hydroxy-Trp.\n12. Aib (the C(CH3)2 residue).\n13. Val, whose carbonyl closes back onto the Cys \u03b1-nitrogen.\n\nThe N-methyl-Lys \u03b5-amine is acylated by CH2C(=O), and that CH2 is attached to the indole nitrogen of the Trp. This forms the second ring, closed in the SMILES with ring label %20.\n\nSMILES: Ic1ccc(cc1)CCCC(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)[C@@H]1CSCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(C(=O)O)cc2)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)C%20)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc3cn%20c4ccccc34)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc5ccc(C(=O)O)cc5)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc6c[nH]c7ccc(O)cc67)C(=O)NC(C)(C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N1)C(N)=O)C(=O)O)C(=O)O"
